			<div class="content" id="post-content-1237067">
									

<p>From a writing standpoint, I can't say it adds anything, and I get the issue with interdependence, but it still irks me that there seems to be a relatively easy fix to an issue and no one's even considered it. If you can reasonably negate the premise, <em>why shouldn't you?</em></p>
<p>As it stands, the SCP has a sibling in <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-910">SCP-910</a> as an unsettling idea, it falls short of being engaging; as it is now it looks like the Foundation tried to research the issue, lost interest, and just put him in a coma to keep him out of his misery. That's not frightening, that's FEMA.</p>
<p>tl;dr I know it's against protocol, but in the larger scope, half of the article would quickly become moot.</p>

